{
  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, known for her claimed psychic abilities and the daughter of one of Europe's longest-reigning monarchs, married Durek Verrett, an American man who identifies as a shaman with a six-generation lineage, on Saturday. Despite the unconventional nature of the royal wedding, crowds still gathered along the streets of Geiranger, hoping to see the bride. Märtha Louise, aged 52 and fourth in line to the Norwegian throne, is the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja. The ceremony was held in a traditional Church of Norway service at the four-star Hotel Union, located in a small village by the Geiranger fjord, and was attended by both royals and celebrities. The princess was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn, whom she had from her previous marriage to Norwegian author Ari Behn, from whom she separated in 2017. Among the roughly 350 guests were her brother Crown Prince Haakon and his wife Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Sweden's Crown Princess Victoria and her husband Prince Daniel, as well as Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Märtha Louise has long deviated from traditional royal norms, having declared herself a clairvoyant and operated a healing school for about ten years, where she guided others in connecting with angels. In 2022, she stepped back from official royal engagements to concentrate on her shared business ventures with Verrett and to create a clearer separation between their activities and the Norwegian royal family. Verrett, who refers to himself on Instagram as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator,' counts Gwyneth Paltrow, the founder of Goop, among his well-known clients, describing her as a 'soul sister.'"
}
```

